+++ b/CONFIG.md
@@ -172,6 +172,17 @@ Miscellaneous:
   the scroll wheel moves the selection. Using the mouse stops the `timeout`
   countdown, as pressing a key does. On BIOS this uses the PS/2 (or emulated
   PS/2) mouse; on UEFI any pointer device the firmware exposes.
+* `gamepad` - If set to `yes`, enable experimental UEFI Xbox 360 controller
+  input in the boot menu. Defaults to `no`. Supports USB `045e:028e`,
+  interface 0 (`ff/5d/01`), interrupt input endpoint `0x81` with 32-byte
+  packets, when the firmware exposes an unclaimed USB IO protocol. D-pad
+  up/down and the vertical left stick move the selection. D-pad right
+  expands directories; D-pad left or B collapses a directory or its parent.
+  A selects an entry. A and B never repeat. A neutral mapped report is
+  required after the menu opens, so release held buttons before navigating.
+  Input stops the `timeout` countdown. Keyboard and mouse input remain
+  available; the entry editor uses keyboard input. This option does not
+  change controller firmware or its operating mode.
 
